These are observable checks, derived from the acceptance criteria and description. They describe WHAT is observed, not how to build it. Make the minimal change that makes all of these true; your accompanying test should assert them:
- When a return trip ticket with a promo code is purchased, the Mozio email confirmation shows a promo code discount amount that is a positive number greater than zero
- When a return trip ticket with a promo code is purchased, the Mozio email confirmation shows the promo code discount name as a non-empty string
- When a one-way trip ticket with a promo code is purchased, the Mozio email confirmation continues to show the promo code discount amount as a positive number greater than zero
- When a return trip ticket with no promo code is purchased, the Mozio email confirmation does not display a promo code discount amount or name

